# One step of the calibration pipeline, run on the server, over a table sent
# whole.
#
# op is one of ComputeOps::cali:
#
#   compute_all                        calculate_result
#   calculate_result_single_round      calculate_result_with_base_distance
#   aggregation_by_distance            aggregation_all_rounds_by_distance
#   auto_detect_noise_bands            remove_nodes_in_band
#   update_table_from_capture
#
# The three SEARCHES (find_min_aggr_single_round, find_min_aggregation_in_window,
# find_distance_for_target_aggregation) are not here. They run for tens of
# seconds and the operator must be able to cancel them, so they are the CaliJob
# action instead. Sending one of them to this service is rejected by name rather
# than blocking the caller for a minute with no way out.
string op

# All 11 round tables plus the form's scalar fields, as CaliTableData JSON. The
# whole table travels because the pipeline writes derived columns back into it --
# the request and the reply are the same document, before and after.
string table_json

string params_json
---
bool success

# The mutated table. The client replaces its display with this; it does not merge,
# and it does not recompute anything from it.
string table_json

# The op's scalar answers -- best distance, removed count, detected bands. "{}"
# for the ops whose only output is the table.
string result_json

string message
